ild).\n\n### Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `cache_system` (structured\n  ephemeral system block, cache-read/write metered via L1); invariant rubric/schema moved into the\n  cached system block for critic_a, reconciler, security judge; Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback carries the\n  marker; default (cache-off) path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 858 passed (854 after EXECUTE, +4 after FIX). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers. R1 GO (default unchanged, fallback caches, the 3 modified test mocks are\n  faithful signature propagation not weakening). R2 GO with a HIGH efficacy finding (W4-R2-1):\n  cached prefixes (65â€“317 tok) are far below Anthropic's per-model minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku\n  4096), so caching silently never fires. FIX iter 1: maximized the stable prefix (moved invariant\n  rubric/schema into system â€” token-multiset identical, F6 fences intact), then GATED the marker\n  behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum` (no dead marker sent) and added honesty-pinning tests.\n  Closure VERIFIER: judge content semantically identical (16/16), gating correct, no-op pin\n  non-vacuous â†’ GO.\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** prompt caching is a **no-op for Aurora's current prompt sizes** â€”\n  all roles' stable prefixes are 15â€“60Ã— below the model minimum. The plumbing is correct and\n  gated; it activates automatically only if a role's stable prefix ever exceeds the minimum. This\n  refines the AuroraTwo research's #1 \"cheap win\" (it was corroboration-only; measured as\n  inapplicable at current sizes). No cost savings banked.\n\n### Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `output_schema` via strict forced\n  tool-use (`emit_result` tool whose input_schema IS the caller schema; SDK has no metering-safe\n  native parse path); shared `CRITIC_VERDICT_SCHEMA`/`REC